# Executive Summary

A controlled incident-response exercise was completed within the Windows enterprise security lab.

The exercise simulated command-line activity, use of a dual-use Windows utility, domain-account creation, and local privilege assignment.

Splunk successfully centralized relevant Windows, Sysmon, and PowerShell telemetry. The activity was investigated, correlated into a timeline, assigned a severity rating, and documented using an incident-response workflow.

Containment and remediation were completed by removing privileged access, deleting the temporary account, and removing test artifacts.

## Outcome
- Incident detected
- Evidence collected
- Timeline created
- Severity assigned
- Containment completed
- Remediation validated
- Incident closed
